TITLE:: TransposeCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that adds an integer to the MIDI note number of each selected note.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::TransposeCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: named CODE::transpose:: that adds an integer number of semitones to each selected note. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies the notes through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::selectedNotes::.

CODE::semitones:: is an LINK::Classes/Integer::. Positive values raise the note, negative values lower it, and zero leaves it unchanged. LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-transpose:: updates the wrapped LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: and, when the note view exists, moves that view by the same number of rows.

LINK::#-beforeImage:: records the previous note number of each note that would move. LINK::#-restore:: moves those notes back with CODE::transpose::, and moves them forward again from LINK::#-afterImage:: on redo. A transposition of zero changes nothing, so it is not an undo step. A note that does not respond to CODE::noteNumber:: and CODE::transpose:: is left out of the image.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::TransposeCommand::. Takes no arguments; transposition is applied by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::TransposeCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: afterImage
The note number now stored on each selected note that responds to CODE::noteNumber:: and CODE::transpose::, after LINK::#-execute::.

ARGUMENT:: args
The same arguments dictionary passed to LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to an event with CODE::\noteNumber::, or CODE::nil:: when no such note was selected.

METHOD:: beforeImage
The note number stored on each selected note before a non-zero integer transposition.

ARGUMENT:: args
The same arguments dictionary about to be passed to LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to an event with CODE::\noteNumber::, or CODE::nil:: when CODE::\semitones:: is not a non-zero LINK::Classes/Integer:: or no selected note can be moved.

METHOD:: execute
Adds CODE::\semitones:: to every note in CODE::\selectedNotes:: that responds to CODE::transpose::.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\selectedNotes:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes) and CODE::\semitones:: (an LINK::Classes/Integer::).

METHOD:: restore
Moves each note to the CODE::\noteNumber:: stored in an image from LINK::#-beforeImage:: or LINK::#-afterImage::, using CODE::transpose:: so the note view slides with it.

ARGUMENT:: image
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to an event with CODE::\noteNumber::, or CODE::nil::.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var note = PianoRollNote(0.0, 60, 100,
	viewFunc: { View() },
	selectFunc: {},
	deselectFunc: {},
	paintFunc: {},
	moveFunc: {}
);
note.stop(1.0);
TransposeCommand.new.execute((
	selectedNotes: [note],
	semitones: -2
));
note.noteNumber; // 58
)
::

PRIVATE:: prEachTarget
